<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mykola Ryabovol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1883">1883</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mykola Ryabovol was a Kuban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> politician and chairman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuban-rada">Kuban Rada</a> in the Kuban People's Republic during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>. He led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> Cossack faction that favoured federation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, bringing conflict with General Denikin's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a>, which sought a united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. He was assassinated in Rostov-on-Don in June 1919.</p></div>
